  "configuration_id": "config_020",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.619 acc, showing that multiprofile + avgpool aggregation is a major driver (+0.092 over singleprofile). Uncertainty: whether avgpool is the optimal aggregation or whether a transformer-based aggregation could capture richer inter-profile structure. This experiment (config_020) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other settings (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) identical to config_018, cleanly isolating the aggregation effect. This is the best next step because aggregation is the critical bottleneck in multiprofile settings—transformer can model non-linear, position-dependent interactions between profiles that simple averaging cannot—and a single-variable comparison directly tells us whether to invest remaining budget in transformer-based configurations or stick with avgpool."
}

